From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorerframe, explorer: ITaskbarList3 progress, overlays, ActivateTab and full-screen windows reach the taskbar

ITaskbarList's ActivateTab and SetActiveAlt and ITaskbarList2's
MarkFullscreenWindow returned E_NOTIMPL (Windows returns S_OK, as Wine's
own tests say), and ITaskbarList3's SetProgressValue, SetProgressState and
SetOverlayIcon returned S_OK and did nothing: downloads, copies and
installers showed no progress on their buttons, chat programs no unread
badge. And the taskbar never posted "TaskbarButtonCreated", which WPF's
TaskbarItemInfo, Qt's QWinTaskbarButton, Chromium and Electron wait for
before they call ITaskbarList3 at all.

- explorerframe sends what a program says about its button to the taskbar
  (Shell_TrayWnd; for an elevated program the session shell's, as
  shell32's notification icons) by WM_COPYDATA. The overlay icon goes as
  its bits, since another process's icon handles cannot be drawn there.
  Unknown progress states are refused with E_INVALIDARG; windows that are
  not there are accepted (S_OK), as on Windows.
- The taskbar draws progress across the button: green, red on an error,
  yellow when paused, a band moving across when indeterminate. A value
  sets the normal state unless the bar is held in error or paused, as
  Windows does; TBPF_NOPROGRESS clears it. A combined button shows the
  progress and overlay of the first of its windows that has one. Both the
  flat and the framed (Horizon, Glass) looks draw them.
- The overlay icon is drawn at the bottom right of the button's icon.
- ActivateTab shows the named window's button as the active one, without
  activating it, until the foreground window changes; SetActiveAlt names
  the button to show as active while the foreground window has none.
- MarkFullscreenWindow: the bar goes behind the window while it is in
  front, as for a window that fills its monitor.
- The taskbar posts "TaskbarButtonCreated" to a window when its button is
  first shown.

Wine's explorerframe tests: the ten todo_wine for ActivateTab and
SetActiveAlt pass and are removed.

Gate: test/taskprogress-gate.sh (Xvfb, the shell's desktop: the button's
pixels for each progress state, the overlay, ActivateTab, the bar's
z-order for a full-screen window, TaskbarButtonCreated). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_TASKBAR_DATA (explorerframe/taskbarlist.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_PROGRESS_PAINT and SG_MUTANT_NO_BUTTON_CREATED
(programs/explorer/systray.c).
